"s-petitions"],"diff":[["=","Competitors"],["-","may"],["+","must"],["=","submit a formal petition to the Event’s Chief Judge to dance at a different skill level than they qualify for in a Jack and Jill division."]]},{"status":"same","key":"s-petitions.1","old_key":"s-petitions.1","old_version":"2019.1A-RPR","sim":1.0,"conf":"high","t":"item","path":["s-petitions"]},{"status":"same","key":"s-petitions.2","old_key":"s-petitions.2","old_version":"2019.1A-RPR","sim":1.0,"conf":"high","t":"item","path":["s-petitions"]},{"status":"changed","key":"s-petitions.3","old_key":"s-petitions.3","old_version":"2019.1A-RPR","sim":1.0,"conf":"high","t":"item","path":["s-petitions"],"diff":[["=","The Chief Judge, or qualified individual(s) designated by the Chief"],["-","Judge ,"],["+","Judge,"],["=","will consider the requested reclassification petition after reviewing the competitor’s Points Registry record."]]},{"status":"same","key":"s-petitions.4","old_key":"s-petitions.4","old_version":"2019.1A-RPR","sim":1.0,"conf":"high","t":"item","path":["s-petitions"]},{"status":"same","key":"s-petitions.5","old_key":"s-petitions.5","old_version":"2019.1A-RPR","sim":1.0,"conf":"high","t":"item","path":["s-petitions"]},{"status":"same","key":"s-petitions~p2","old_key":"s-petitions~p2","old_version":"2019.1A-RPR","sim":1.0,"conf":"high","t":"para","path":["s-petitions"]},{"status":"changed","key":"table-wsdc-skill-level-jack-and-jill-advancement-chart","old_key":"table-wsdc-skill-level-jack-and-jill-advancement-chart","old_version":"2019.1A-RPR","sim":0.936,"conf":"high","t":"table","path":["s-petitions"],"diff":[["=","WSDC Skill Level Jack and Jill Advancement Chart | WSDC Notes | Allowed | Required Skill Level | Dancers may use the petition process to request dancing up or down one level in a competition. Dancers and promoter should realize the risks associated with granting petitions up or down. | Dancers who reach these point milestones are given the option to move up. Dancers should realize the risks associated with dancing at a higher skill level. | Dancers who reach these point milestones are required to move up. The intent is to instruct excellent dancers that they must advance to the next level. Champion | Champion points are tracked in the Points Registry; however, Champion is a general category that is set by promoters for their higher skill level dancers in attendance. | Champion Dancer Allowed to"],["-","dance based on event criteria set by Event Promoter | Required to enter if meets criteria set by Event Promoter"],["+","move up with 150 All Star points (no time limit)"],["=","All Star | All Star is intended to be extremely competitive, with constantly evolving and changing skill level. Dancers require consistent placements to remain in this category. | All Star Dancer Must receive 3 All Star points in last 36 Months to remain in All Star Allowed to compete in Advanced or All Star with 1 or 2 All Star points | Must receive 10 Advanced points in a 12 month period to move back to All Star Advanced | Advanced is intended to be very competitive where dancers move up from Intermediate or return to from All Star. | Allowed to move up with 45 Advanced points accumulated within 36 Months | Required to move up with 60 Advanced points accumulated within 36 Months Advanced Dancer Intermediate | Intermediate is for dancers who are perfecting their social and competitive dance skills. | Allowed to move up with 30+ Intermediate points | Required to move up with 45+ Intermediate points Intermediate Dancer Novice | Novice is where dancers demonstrate their basic dance skills. | Allowed to move up with 16+ Novice points | Required to move up with 30+ Novice points Novice Dancer Newcomer | Some events offer a Newcomer division."],["-","It"],["+","New dancers / competitors should check the event’s rules – it"],["=","may be mandatory for new dancers / competitors."],["-","New dancers / competitors should check the event’s rules."],["=","| | Newcomer Dancer"]]},{"status":"added","key":"s-specific-rules-regarding-competitor-divisions-and-points.10","t":"item","path":["s-specific-rules-regarding-competitor-divisions-and-points"],"text":"Registry Events must allow All Stars who have a minimum of 150 All Star points to compete in a WSDC Champion Jack & Jill contest."},{"status":"added","key":"s-specific-rules-regarding-competitor-divisions-and-points.10a","t":"item","path":["s-specific-rules-regarding-competitor-divisions-and-points"],"text":"Registry Events may include additional qualifications (e.g., predefined number of Champion / Invitational points, NASDE Classic or Showcase placement(s), professional staff at event) for their WSDC Champion J&J contest, but must allow All Stars who have 150+ All Star points to compete."},{"status":"added","key":"s-specific-rules-regarding-competitor-divisions-and-points.10b","t":"item","path":["s-specific-rules-regarding-competitor-divisions-and-points"],"text":"All Stars who qualify are not required to compete in Champions."},{"status":"added","key":"s-specific-rules-regarding-competitor-divisions-and-points.10c","t":"item","path":["s-specific-rules-regarding-competitor-divisions-and-points"],"text":"Competitors who do not meet the Registry Event’s qualifications for Champions or All Stars, even if they have Champion points, must submit a petition and receive approval to dance in the appropriate division."},{"status":"added","key":"s-the-competitor.4a","t":"item","path":["s-recording-points-responsibilities","s-the-competitor"],"text":"Competitors may compete as a Leader / Follower in a skill level Jack and Jill contest and as a Follower / Leader (in the opposite role) in an age-based level Jack and Jill and/or other contest(s), if permitted by the Registry Event."},{"status":"added","key":"s-the-competitor.5a","t":"item","path":["s-recording-points-responsibilities","s-the-competitor"],"text":"Competitors who do not meet the Registry Event’s qualifications for Champions or All Stars, even if they have Champion points, must submit a petition and receive approval to dance in the appropriate division."}]}